      "text": [
        "01 / CREATIVE PROPOSITION",
        "An illustrated memoir in motion",
        ".json  /  VIDEO SYSTEM                                           01",
        "Video design & production architecture",
        "Move like a memory.",
        "Sound like a confession.",
        "Open like a rabbit hole.",
        "A Codex-ready prototype built from existing chapter concept boards."
      ]
    },
    {
      "slide": 2,
      "text": [
        "02 / CREATIVE STRATEGY",
        "Our content has three jobs",
        ".json  /  VIDEO SYSTEM                                           02",
        "READ",
        "The chapter is canonical.",
        "Narrative pacing & ambiguity.",
        "EXPLORE",
        "Illustration, motion, sound and",
        "archival context.",
        "REVISIT",
        "Older thinking, contradictions",
        "and revision traces.",
        "One emotional universe, different media. The video is a doorway—not a substitute for the book."
      ]
    },
    {
      "slide": 3,
      "text": [
        "03 / PROPOSED FORMAT STRATEGY",
        "A production mix with reuse built in",
        ".json  /  VIDEO SYSTEM                                           03",
        "75%",
        "Illustrated motion",
        "Recognizable portals • parallax • quote cards",
        "20%",
        "Authentic archival",
        "Real photographs and recordings with permission",
        "5%",
        "Realistic AI scenes",
        "Only for dreams / reconstructions, clearly contextualized",
        "These ratios are the initial creative hypothesis; pilot results should decide future allocation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "slide": 4,
      "text": [
        "04 / ART DIRECTION",
        "Visual grammar: quiet luxury x graphic memory",
        ".json  /  VIDEO SYSTEM                                           04",
        "CUT PAPER",
        "4–8 slow layers",
        "LIGHT",
        "Soft dusk / practical lamps",
        "TYPOGRAPHY",
        "Archival serif + small metadata",
        "COLOR",
        "Midnight navy / cream / warm coral",
        "MOTION",
        "Subtle, never cartoonish"
      ]
    },
    {
      "slide": 5,
      "text": [
        "05 / 45-SECOND EPISODE BLUEPRINT",
        "One video = one emotional arc",
        ".json  /  VIDEO SYSTEM                                           05",
        "00–05",
        "HOOK",
        "One unresolved image / line",
        "05–14",
        "ENTER",
        "Move through the chapter portal",
        "14–28",
        "REMEMBER",
        "Stay with a concrete scene",
        "28–39",
        "RECONSIDER",
        "Reveal a tension, not a moral",
        "39–45",
        "RETURN",
        "Book + chapter invitation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "slide": 6,
      "text": [
        "06 / MOTION CHOREOGRAPHY",
        "Make the portal feel alive, not busy",
        ".json  /  VIDEO SYSTEM                                           06",
        "•",
        "Slow depth movement and deliberate reveals",
        "•",
        "Scale shifts: 2–5% per 5–8 seconds",
        "•",
        "Gentle ambient light and material grain",
        "•",
        "Voiceover comes first; music is supportive",
        "•",
        "No aggressive spinning, lip-sync or fake realism"
      ]
    },
    {
      "slide": 7,
      "text": [
        "07 / HUMAN INTIMACY",
        "Chapter prototype A — Cold Rice",
        ".json  /  VIDEO SYSTEM                                           07",
        "HERO",
        "Bowl / family table",
        "Animate drifting steam, the warm pool of light, and the slow arrival of the ring. The ordinary gesture is the emotional engine."
      ]
    },
    {
      "slide": 8,
      "text": [
        "08 / IDENTITY OVER DISPLAY",
        "Chapter prototype B — Fashion",
        ".json  /  VIDEO SYSTEM                                           08",
        "HERO",
        "Shoes → wardrobe → self",
        "Use Air Jordan 1 and an iconic Adidas as personal history; avoid commercial advertising aesthetics. Fade from consumer noise into timeless materials."
      ]
    },
    {
      "slide": 9,
      "text": [
        "09 / BECOMING & BELONGING",
        "Chapter prototype C — To Saigon",
        ".json  /  VIDEO SYSTEM                                           09",
        "HERO",
        "Ba Son / dusk / still here",
        "Return to the sunset: a couple viewed from behind, pink cap and blonde hair, Gấu nearby. Preserve the skyline and emotional quiet."
      ]
    },
    {
      "slide": 10,
      "text": [
        "10 / ASSET SYSTEM",
        "A chapter is a repeatable production unit",
        ".json  /  VIDEO SYSTEM                                           10",
        "•",
        "Approved flattened board (source of truth)",
        "•",
        "Separated transparent portal planes",
        "•",
        "Episode script + narrated audio + captions",
        "•",
        "Motion timeline JSON + music / SFX ledger",
        "•",
        "9:16 social master, 16:9 archive, still cover",
        "•",
        "Rights, consent, accuracy and author sign-off"
      ]
    },
    {
      "slide": 11,
      "text": [
        "11 / CODEX WORKFLOW",
        "Build once. Adapt 32 times.",
        ".json  /  VIDEO SYSTEM                                           11",
        "01",
        "Inventory and approve art",
        "02",
        "Isolate layered rings",
        "03",
        "Create chapter timeline",
        "04",
        "Narrate and caption",
        "05",
        "Render formats & review",
        "Starter code includes a working flattened-board motion prototype; real parallax requires layered asset extraction."
      ]
    },
    {
      "slide": 12,
      "text": [
        "12 / PRODUCTION ROADMAP",
        "Pilot, measure, then scale",
        ".json  /  VIDEO SYSTEM                                           12",
        "SPRINT 1",
        "Lock identity and build one visual template.",
        "Produce Cold Rice prototype.",
        "SPRINT 2",
        "Fashion + To Saigon variants.",
        "Caption, audio and template QA.",
        "SPRINT 3",
        "Test across channels, compare retention",
